invariant: INV-17
file: sha256_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha256_of_hw returns without wiping the context it hashed in, so its
  dead frame keeps the end of the input and the digest's eight words.
  HMAC hashes a key longer than a block through this call, and the bytes
  left are the key's last ones and the value HMAC then uses as its key.
  The digest is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test
  copies the stack below one sha256_of_hw call and looks for four
  schedule, message or state words in a row. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    sha256_final_hw(&s, out);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    sha256_final_hw(&s, out);
